  "_comment": "Gem frames (GDD §6.2). A frame is a recipe, not code (docs/M1_PLAN.md D33): it names which registered effect atoms it rolls and the range each rolls in, per tier. All ten frames are here. Every one carries a real drawback, which §6.2 requires and §10 explains: a pure upgrade creates a known-correct ranking, which is exactly the meta this design exists to avoid. Ranges are provisional and are the first thing the S8 balance pass moves. Two frames read their own per-fight counters rather than a rolled range — CHARGE stores on a kill and SPEND consumes what it stored — so their paired atoms roll fixed values.",
